# SALGIN alone, a win by KO: Up (the flying kick, 2 points) held from the
# start. Windows' key repeat (500/33 ms) presses it again every 33 ms, so a
# new kick starts as soon as the latches clear (each move is 3 beats of
# 200 ms); in range (the opponent walks in to 69-100 px) every kick lands.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame salgin --headless --ms 60000 --input tools/play/salgin-alone-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame salgin --headless --ms 63000 --fix all --input tools/play/salgin-alone-win.input
#
# The opponent's energy is below 1 on the beat at 51200 in both versions;
# the hold ends after it (the keys are locked from the KO) and before the
# window closes, 30 end ticks later (54821). The player keeps 82 energy,
# 8200 points; in the Corrigida, whose round starts 2050 ms later, S5's
# single seed (from that clock) picks other attacks: 83, 8300 points.

# The Corrigida (`--fix all`) shows SALGIN's controls screen first; Enter takes
# it down 50 ms after it opened, PORRADA stands for 2 s (the frozen intro,
# `fight_controls.start_delay_ms`) and the round then plays as the
# Original's from its start, 2050 ms later (`delay`: every later line
# moves too).
# Its keys are the new layout: S is the flying kick (voadora) (the Original's Up).
0 ?fight_keys_asdf keymap up s
50 ?fight_controls_screen key return
50 ?fight_controls_screen delay 2050
300 hold up 52000
1000 dump start
20000 dump fight
53000 dump won
56000 result won 8200 | won 8300
